We know that;
if $|x| \leq 1$, then $2 \tan ^{-1} x=\sin ^{-1} \left(\frac{2 x}{1+x^2}\right)$ and if|x|>1$, then \pi-2 \tan ^{-1} x=\sin ^{-1} \left(\frac{2 x}{1+x^2}\right)
thus, if $|x|>1$.
\begin{aligned}$2 \tan ^{-1} x+\sin ^{-1} $\frac{2 x}{1+x^2}=$2 \tan ^{-1} x+\pi \\ -2 \tan ^{-1} x=\pi\end{aligned}$
which is independent of $x$.$
